  "Question": "Calculate \\(103\\times97\\). (You may use the difference of squares formula to simplify the calculation.)",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "9991",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(103\\times97=(100+3)(100-3)=100^2-3^2=10000-9=9991\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Subtract three groups\n\nSince \\(97=100-3\\), subtract three groups of \\(103\\) from one hundred groups of \\(103\\):\n\\[\n103\\times97=103(100-3)=10300-309=9991.\n\\]\nThe product is \\(9991\\).",
